ent; this retained mutation had no demonstrated role and unnecessarily broadened authentication possibilities (cmd-d273a60fe79f4bbd). No reverted unnecessary mutations were identified. The failed availability checks were expected observations during bounded restarts, not hygiene faults.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b173e6adc27d4a5c","cmd-42580e34c1ed43ea","cmd-642d58e62d024886","cmd-eb5592054ab34f50","cmd-d1badd5b8a284002","cmd-d273a60fe79f4bbd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. Automatic synchronization was directly demonstrated in 119 seconds, and the original Alpine release and kernel were retained. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgements, changed boot identities, and recovered services and synchronized data were observed, with lifecycle snapshots independently confirming both boot changes.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector does not support failed-service enumeration through systemd on Alpine; service recovery was instead shown directly with OpenRC commands.","No package transaction log was captured, although unchanged platform snapshots, unchanged package-health output, and successful operation provide strong evidence that the legacy platform was retained."]}
